# SFT execution status v0.87

2026-09-13. Fixed generator worker, private packet transport, generator source
installation and the internal generation-to-import pipeline now have local
implementation and synthetic tests. Gate 5 remains incomplete. This is work
within the existing checkpoint-import task, not an additional roadmap gate.

## Completed in this step

- Fixed generator entry: 16 tests. Authenticates entry/helper/source bytes,
  stages private source copies, bypasses initializer autoregistration, calls
  the fixed tiny generator once and writes one private success packet.
- Private packet codec: 18 tests. Checks exact synthetic metadata, 736-parameter
  configuration, inventories, fixed trainer/tokenizer placeholders and
  source-copy receipts; rejects tampering, malformed encodings and excess size.
- Generator bootstrap: 19 tests. Fixed Linux worker/arguments/environment,
  root-only software mount, private scratch, privilege/descriptor reduction
  and guardian-controlled release.
- Generator guardian: 27 tests. Parent/deadline watch before release, bounded
  private transport, worker exit/EOF, one kill, empty cgroup and removal.
  Both socket endpoints are configured/read back before forks and rechecked
  before release. Missing buffer capacity fails closed.
- Generator source add-on: 14 tests. Exact pinned helper, absent destinations,
  full pre-write bounds, tracked owned writes and freeze. Started failures
  taint the fresh software tree; prior files are never overwritten.
- Internal pipeline: 23 tests. Connects generator -> codec -> controls ->
  separate fresh import layout -> existing guarded launcher exactly once.
  Only aggregate hashes/counts leave the pipeline. Success explicitly means
  two guardian passes with whole-harness cleanup still pending.

All 117 new tests plus 292 regression tests pass on Python 3.11.15 and 3.13.7:
409 tests per runtime, with no failures, errors or skips. Final test processes
had audit hooks denying network/process/native-library calls and ML imports.
No denied operation was attempted and no ML module was loaded. All 12 new
Python files pass syntax and 100-column checks. Ruff was unavailable.

Tests exercise the actual frozen metadata writer using in-memory filesystem
doubles, packet encoding/decoding, actual controls builder, doubled layout
filesystem and actual launch validators with guardian doubles. One generator
receipt roundtrip uses its own generated tempfile with only the tensor generator
and runtime gate doubled. None of these is native tensor-generation, isolation,
kernel containment or full-size import evidence.

## Review corrections completed

Parent paths now require different parent device/inode identities as well as
non-overlapping lexical paths, rejecting same-parent bind-mount aliases.
The shared deadline is rechecked after root preflight and immediately before
import-layout writes. The full generator lifecycle/resource/nonclaim receipt
is mandatory, including one kill and verified reaping. Regression tests cover
these cases and failures after generation, during installation and import.

## Exact remaining work before native qualification

1. Add identity-tracked cleanup for external checkpoint/tokenizer/output and
   mountpoint trees, including partial installation and failed workers.
   Frozen OwnedRootfs cleanup does not own these sibling trees.
2. Update the standalone accepted-runtime harness and fresh pinned host-source
   admission, preserving authenticated-loader namespaces and a single exact
   OwnedRootfs class identity. Bind that harness to independent supervision.
3. Then run and verify the generated-only Linux qualification with the required
   execution approval. The current internal pipeline is not a standalone CLI,
   does not perform acquisition or whole-harness cleanup, and is not run here.

After qualification, the existing dedicated-host/runtime, external-writer
exclusion, full-size resource admission and real checkpoint CPU import remain,
then the documented GPU-worker/private-data/CUDA-smoke and SFT prerequisites.

Worker packets are capped at 65,536 bytes, outer private envelopes at 131,072
bytes and verified socket buffers at a minimum of 262,144 bytes. These are
separate transport bounds. Scratch/shm capacities and generated final-size
limits are not cumulative write accounting. The pipeline's 240-second shared
deadline is cooperative and still requires an independent hard supervisor.
No GPU is needed for the outstanding cleanup/admission/supervisor code.

All new files remain local. Prior source/evidence bindings are preserved; no
tracked/staged diff, CI change, commit or push was made. No actual model,
tokenizer or dataset payload, network/S3/instance, GPU, inference, native Linux
worker or training operation occurred. Public real import remains closed at
host_guard_not_bound. Execution permission, training authorization and
production eligibility remain false.

